  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14214505/assets/89445981059ca7902f22c916f7241573dcfa8b70798b067896b9a30d0913d251.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-2,5].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x)$, the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $3$ and $9,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-2,5]$ given that $f(5)=10.$",
